    "text": "Randolph County, North Carolina\n4 injured in Randolph County car crash; one child has serious injuries, troopers say\n1 days ago\nRANDOLPH COUNTY, N.C. — UPDATE: North Carolina State Highway Patrol shared more details about yesterday's crash in Randolph County. Troopers responded to a two-vehicle collision that occurred on N.C. Highway 49 at Low Bridge Road just before 10am Monday. They say one driver was traveling south in a 2019 Chevrolet pickup. Another driver was traveling from Low Bridge Road across 49 in a 2006 Chevrolet SUV. Woodruff and Walker collided in the intersection. Walker sustained minor injuries, however, was not transported. Woodruff and two minor passengers were transported to Moses Cone Hospital. An additional minor passenger of Woodruff’s was transported to UNC for serious injuries. Currently, the investigation remains ongoing, and no charges have been made.",
